The code statements that lead to the bug are:
if (status & rx_not_ls)
    return priv->dma_conf.dma_buf_sz;
Reason:
This condition assumes that for all non-last descriptors, buf2 is always fully filled (dma_buf_sz). On GMAC4 with split header enabled, hardware may not fill buf2 of the first descriptor, causing the length of buf2 for the second descriptor to be calculated incorrectly and leading to a kernel oops.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
if (priv->plat->core_type != DWMAC_CORE_GMAC4 && (status & rx_not_ls))
    return priv->dma_conf.dma_buf_sz;
/* GMAC4 or last descriptor */
plen = stmmac_get_rx_frame_len(priv, p, coe);
return plen - len;
Reason:
For GMAC4 (or any last descriptor), the fix always computes the actual payload length from the descriptor using `stmmac_get_rx_frame_len`, which correctly handles cases where buf2 may not be fully filled. This prevents incorrect length calculation and the subsequent oops.

